{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Introduce exported wrapper types around the underlying protobuf ConfigGroup values (e.g., ChannelGroup, ApplicationGroup, OrdererGroup, ConsortiumsGroup, ConsortiumGroup, Organization) that hold pointers into the base/updated *cb.Config trees; ConfigTx exposes accessors such as Application(), Orderer(), Consortiums(), and Organization(name) so calls can be chained as c.Application().Organization(\"Org1\").SetAnchorPeer(...).",
    "All AddXXX and UpdateXXX functions are renamed to SetXXX; SetXXX functions overwrite existing map values (policies, capabilities, ACLs, MSP values) without error. For slice-backed values (anchor peers, orderer endpoints), Set replaces the element with the same identifying key (e.g., host:port) if present and appends otherwise, guaranteeing no duplicates are added.",
    "ConfigTx.Base() is renamed to BaseConfig() and ConfigTx.Updated() is renamed to UpdatedConfig(), with GoDocs updated to describe that they return the original and the modified config protos respectively.",
    "A new subpackage configtx/orderer holds only the orderer-related types (Orderer, BatchSize, Kafka, EtcdRaft, ConsensusState); no orderer.Policies map type is created because policy helpers are shared across scopes and remain in configtx.",
    "A new subpackage configtx/membership holds the MSP-related types (MSP, SigningIdentityInfo, OUIdentifier, CryptoConfig, NodeOUs); functions stay in configtx unless they operate purely on membership types.",
    "All RemoveXXX functions become idempotent: a missing value is a no-op and the error return is removed from their signatures; all call sites, tests, and examples are updated accordingly.",
    "The GoDoc overhaul removes the eight listed trivial examples, renames Example_xxx functions to intent-revealing names, splits large examples into focused ones (e.g., Example_policyRetrieval, Example_ordererUpdate, Example_membership), drops Output: validation so examples compile but are not output-verified, and wraps long lines so generated docs need no horizontal scrolling.",
    "The CLI is implemented as a single Go command using the cobra/pflag libraries already vendored in the repository, with subcommands for generating a system channel genesis block, generating an application channel creation transaction, and computing config updates; each updatable property (anchor peers, orderer endpoints, policies, capabilities, consortiums, ACLs, MSPs, batch size) is exposed via flags/subcommands, and input/output are protobuf files.",
    "No backward-compatibility shims are kept: the library API is changed in place and all in-repo callers are updated to compile, but migrating configtxgen to the new CLI is out of scope."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The target is the existing Hyperledger Fabric Go configtx library (pkg/config) with roughly 30-40 exported Add/Update/Remove/Get functions plus comprehensive unit tests and examples that already exist and must be modified in place.",
    "A working Go development environment, the vendored fabric repository, and the ability to run go test, go vet, gofmt, and godoc locally are available from day one.",
    "Effort figures are workdays of one developer and include implementation, unit test updates/creation, and GoDoc updates within each activity's scope; they exclude calendar waiting time for CI queues and reviewer availability, but include time to address review feedback.",
    "Only the Go API surface changes; the underlying protobuf message definitions (cb.Config, cb.ConfigGroup, etc.) are untouched.",
    "The CLI lives inside the fabric repository (e.g., under cmd/ or a samples directory) and only needs to satisfy the demo acceptance criteria; production-grade features (YAML profiles, full configtxgen parity) are not required.",
    "Stories U4 and U5 are type moves only: shared helper functions for policies/capabilities remain in configtx, and only references, imports, tests, and examples are adjusted.",
    "For U3, existing ConfigTx-level methods may delegate to the new chained subtype methods to avoid duplicating logic, and the examples/tests are rewritten to the chained style.",
    "The developer is proficient in Go and protocol buffers but needs some ramp-up time on the existing configtx codebase and Fabric conventions (Gerrit workflow, GoDoc style)."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Codebase analysis and overall API/package design",
      "activity_description": "Study the existing configtx package, its functions, tests, and examples; inventory all Add/Update/Remove functions to be converted; design the chained-API wrapper types (U3), the orderer and membership subpackage layouts (U4/U5), the idempotent-remove signature changes (U6), and the CLI command tree (U8); produce a short design note to anchor implementation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Convert Add/Update functions to Set semantics",
      "activity_description": "Rename all AddXXX/UpdateXXX functions in configtx to SetXXX and change behavior to overwrite existing values instead of erroring; implement replace-or-append logic for slice-based values such as anchor peers and orderer endpoints so no duplicates occur; update unit tests (including removal of now-invalid 'already exists' error cases), affected examples, and GoDocs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2: Rename Base() and Updated() to BaseConfig() and UpdatedConfig()",
      "activity_description": "Rename the ConfigTx.Base() and ConfigTx.Updated() methods, update all call sites in the library, tests, and examples, and revise their GoDocs to clearly describe the returned original and updated configs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3: Implement chainable subtype API",
      "activity_description": "Create the intermediary wrapper types (Application, Orderer, Consortiums, Consortium, Organization, and channel-level wrappers) holding references to the underlying ConfigGroup protos; move/attach getters and setters to these types so calls like c.Application().Organization(name).SetAnchorPeer(...) work; refactor existing ConfigTx-level functions to delegate; update all unit tests and examples to the chained style and update GoDocs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4: Create orderer subpackage for orderer types",
      "activity_description": "Create the configtx/orderer package; move the Orderer, BatchSize, Kafka, EtcdRaft, and ConsensusState types into it; update all references, imports, tests, and examples across the library; write package-level GoDoc documenting the orderer types.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5: Create membership subpackage for MSP types",
      "activity_description": "Create the configtx/membership package; move the MSP, SigningIdentityInfo, OUIdentifier, CryptoConfig, and NodeOUs types into it; update all references, imports, tests, and examples across the library; write package-level GoDoc documenting the membership types.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6: Make Remove functions idempotent",
      "activity_description": "Change all RemoveXXX functions so removing a non-existent value is a silent no-op; remove the error return from their signatures where it is no longer needed; update every call site, unit test, and example to the new signatures and document the behavior in GoDocs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7: GoDoc and example overhaul",
      "activity_description": "Remove the eight listed trivial examples; write improved documentation for configtx.New(); rename Example_xxx functions to intent-revealing names; add new focused examples (e.g., Example_policyRetrieval, Example_ordererUpdate, Example_membership); strip Output validation from examples; insert line breaks so no GoDoc code block scrolls horizontally; verify rendered output locally via godoc -http=:2020.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8: Build configtx demo CLI",
      "activity_description": "Implement a cobra-based CLI with commands/flags to generate a system channel genesis block, generate an application channel creation transaction, and compute config updates for all updatable properties (anchor peers, orderer endpoints, policies, capabilities, consortiums, ACLs, MSPs, batch size) via flags/subcommands; implement protobuf file input/output (e.g., --config and --output handling as in the acceptance example); write help/manual documentation and unit tests for the command logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Integration and regression verification",
      "activity_description": "Run the full package unit test suite, go vet, gofmt, and lint checks; resolve cross-story integration issues (e.g., CLI and examples built on the final Set/chained/idempotent-remove API); verify GoDoc rendering end to end and smoke-test the CLI commands against sample config protos.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Code review and rework",
      "activity_description": "Prepare changes for submission (commit structure, messages), respond to reviewer feedback across the API refactor, new packages, docs, and CLI, apply requested changes, and re-run affected tests until changes are approved.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 38.5
  }
}

